ng  made of humble chipboard  it creates a sacred atmosphere akin to a  gothic cathedral  and this is an essential criterion for  spirituality is that you don't recognize  where the light's coming from the inner  shell and the outer shell are not  identical there's something in between  whatever that is the holy spirit our  dear lord something else that was our  light motif from the outset  motorway churches are a predominantly  german phenomenon  the first gas station for the soul was  built 50 years ago  now there are total of 40 across germany  here you can recover from the stresses  and strains of autobahn driving  these churches are not affiliated with  any one denomination  and are architecturally pretty way out  so  who really uses them  nowadays people come from all around the  world in the summer a lot of people came  on foot or by bike and they stopped off  here it was very important to us that  this was an interfaith church open to  everyone  and literally open 24 7.  people frequently come here in the  middle of the night or to friday prayers  sometimes they pen moving life stories  in the visitors book about separations  they've been through or accidents  they've recovered from  the kings of the road can take away free  copies of the trucker's bible  the church is popular with the public  it's absolutely beautiful something  really special  the church was funded by donations and  in contrast to many other churches these  days people do come here  it's up to them what they see in it  both my partner and i believe in  buildings that can't be easily  categorized  this is a wonderful place to take some  time out  before rejoining the fray  you
 

